            <ArticleTitle>Accelerated coronary artery stenosis at a site proximal to coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rapid progression of coronary stenosis has been described in patients undergoing percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA), typically resulting in symptomatic angina 3 to 30 months postprocedure. We report a case of accelerated coronary stenosis in the instrumented vessel resulting in angina 3 days post-PTCA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
